      "Enable only the required project APIs for private DNS and IAP if disabled. Before VM spend verify control of the qualification DNS records, TLS path, tagged build digests, scoped IAM, authenticated synthetic ingress and automatic teardown. Record all new resource IDs.",
      "Create the isolated target described above; at most two E2 VMs, two regional data volumes, one dedicated frontend service (maximum two instances, two containers each), one NAT IP and one public qualification forwarding rule. Add only the qualification DNS/TLS records, roles scoped to dedicated resources or identities, independent monitor and notification channel.",
      "Run the restart, fencing, off-host backup/restore and host-loss tests with synthetic fixtures. Up to one verification message, one test alert and its recovery notification to the active Google account only. Amir acknowledges in the drill.",
      "Stop sooner on uncertainty about costs/traffic, control failure or unexpected effects. Schedule the time bound and verify it before load. Keep 10,000 synthetic requests and 2 GiB NAT processing as planning limits. Do not start infrastructure if bounded traffic, egress, cleanup and remaining headroom cannot be established.",
      "At cutoff remove only the recorded qualification resources including VMs, disks except the seven-day backup, network/LB, qualification DNS/cert, IAM bindings, service accounts, build source copies, dedicated image digests, monitors and channel. Retire unused newly enabled services only if safe for all other users of the project; otherwise retain enabled API and record it. Delete the synthetic backup by Nov 26 at 4 p.m. PST and verify final inventory."
